//@version=6
indicator("UCTPROBE_I6AN4_IF6", overlay = false)

// I6a-N4 (2026-11-07), capture row I6A-N4-1c: `docs/pine/capture-queue-2026-11-07-i6a-n4.md`.
// The question is whether TradingView COMPILES this file. Ours refuses it `pine:indent` (master SERVED it on both lanes, drawing close on up bars). COMPILE FAILS = our refusal is right. COMPILES = N01 says what the line at indent 6 did (close on up bars = read as a block).
// Record isFailed() and, if it fails, status().errorDescription.editorError (code, message,
// line, column): that text IS the measurement. Paste each file ALONE (a Pine script compiles
// as a whole, so one invalid shape would hide the others).
// Indents are SPACES, counted exactly; do not let the editor re-indent on paste.

m = bar_index % 2
k = bar_index % 3
v = open
if close > open
      v := close
plot(v, "N01_if_body_at_6")
